<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Magenta</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1859">1859</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-italian-war-of-independence">Second Italian War of Independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Magenta was fought on 4 June 1859 near Magenta in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-italian-war-of-independence">Second Italian War of Independence</a>. A French army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon-iii">Napoleon III</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patrice-de-macmahon">Patrice de MacMahon</a>, with Sardinian support, defeated the Austrians under Ferenc Gyulai, who abandoned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>. MacMahon was made Duke of Magenta, and the new magenta dye was named after the battle.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-magenta.jpg" alt="Battle of Magenta" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adolphe Yvon · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adolphe_Yvon_-_Batalla_de_Magenta.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>France and Piedmont defeated it at <b>Magenta</b> and Solferino in 1859, and in 1866 the Prussian army, using breech-loading rifles and railways, crushed it at the Battle of Königgrätz on 3 July.</blockquote><a href="/empire/austrian-empire">Austrian Empire · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>In alliance with Napoleon III of France, Sardinia defeated Austria in 1859 at <b>Magenta</b> and Solferino and gained Lombardy; in 1860 plebiscites joined Tuscany, Parma, Modena and the Romagna, while Savoy and Nice were ceded to France as the price of French support.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>A contingent sent to the Crimean War in 1855 restored its standing, and with French help it won at <b>Magenta</b> and Solferino in 1859.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-sardinia">Kingdom of Sardinia · Military</a></li></ul></section>
